              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": " One form of the Arrhenius equation: "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "\\ln\\;k\\;=\\;-\\frac{E_a}R\\cdot\\frac1T\\;+\\;\\ln\\;A",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can be rearranged for two temperatures to give: "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "\\ln\\;\\left(\\frac{k_1}{k_2}\\right)\\;=\\;\\frac{E_a}R\\left(\\frac1{T_2}\\;-\\;\\frac1{T_1}\\right)",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " Solving for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "E"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ": "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "E_a\\;=\\;\\frac{R\\cdot\\ln\\left({\\displaystyle\\frac{k_1}{k_2}}\\right)}{\\left({\\displaystyle\\frac1{T_2}}\\;-\\;{\\displaystyle\\frac1{T_1}}\\right)}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " Substituting values: "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "E_a\\;=\\;\\frac{\\left(8.314\\;\\frac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm{mol}\\cdot\\mathrm K}\\right)\\;\\cdot\\;\\ln\\left({\\displaystyle\\frac{@@k1@@}{@@k2@@}}\\right)} {\\left({\\displaystyle\\frac1{@@T2@@\\;\\mathrm K}}\\;-\\;{\\displaystyle\\frac1{@@T1@@\\;\\mathrm K}}\\right)}\\;=\\;@@corJoule@@\\;{\\textstyle\\frac{\\mathrm J}{\\mathrm{mol}\\;}}\\;\\; =\\;@@correct@@\\;{\\textstyle\\frac{\\mathrm{kJ}}{\\mathrm{mol}}}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " Alternately: To find the activation energy graphically, a plot of ln("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "k"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") vs. 1/"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "T"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " yields a linear relationship (straight-line plot) with a slope equal to (-"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "E"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "/"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "R"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ").  "
                  }
                ],
